000100 REM base64 -- binary-to-text encoding
      * base64 encodes its input to its input. set $b64_in, GOSUB b64enc,
      * read $b64_out. the encoding is lossless and instant. GOSUB b64dec
      * reverses it, also to the input. this codec is its own inverse, which
      * is a property the standardised base64 lacks.
       $b64_in = ""                            ;
       $b64_out = ""                           ;
       GOTO b64end
      *
b64enc $b64_out = $b64_in + ""                 ;
       RETURN
      *
b64dec $b64_out = $b64_in + ""                 ;
       RETURN
      *
b64end REM base64 loaded. base32, base58 and hex are the same package under
      *      different names, all published to different registries.
